          "total_blocked_by": 0,
          "blocking": 0,
          "total_blocking": 0
        },
        "body": "I'd like to ask for a few things:\n\n* currently, if I delete an API Client the tokens are gone. That really sucks because they're the most tedious thing to replace. One solution here that I'd be particularly partial to is is to create token groups and then be able to apply token groups to API Clients. This would both allow mass updating of different clients' tokens *AND* would allow for easy rebuilds.\n* currently, I find myself duplicating API Clients for different scenarios - localhost, staging, prod. It'd be nice if I could just have multiple tokens for the same API Client so I only have to implement the exact correct permissions structure once.\n* currently, you can't duplicate an API Client token. It'd be nice to be able to do that.",
